title the readlink and sed sites, and a counsel piece on the instrument
prompt Keaton said kg the readlink and sed sites, then asked for a counsel writing and a send, and for a readiness answer on restarting the Dream outer loop.
think The readlink ruling came out of each script's own subject rather than a preference. agent-jail.sh runs bubblewrap over a Linux kernel and a /nix store; pier_nixos_track.sh rewrites /etc/nixos as root. Neither has a bench where it runs and GNU readlink is absent, so both declare that and keep the GNU spelling -- gate where the requirement is known. one_clock_zone_scan.sh and ryekey_control.sh cross to the second pier, so both take the helper.
think resolve_path asks the shell rather than the tool: cd plus pwd -P, following one symlink hop. BSD readlink carried no -f for most of its life and macOS gained one only recently, so reaching for -f bets on the age of the second bench rather than a spelling both accept. One hop is what every caller here needs; a full resolver would have to bound its own recursion, and that bound has no measurement behind it.
think sed_inplace exists because the two dialects have NO overlap -- GNU takes no argument after -i, BSD requires a backup suffix. A temp file copied back through the original inode runs everywhere and keeps the tracked mode, which mv would lose and the exec-bit law would then book.
think The three sed sites plant refusals into throwaway pens, so a broken plant reads exactly like a passing guard. That made the behavioural check the only honest one: both caravan witnesses ran and still read widened=refused and rounding=refused.
obs The helper control proves by doing rather than counting: resolve_path compared against this host's own readlink -f on six real paths including a symlink-to-directory and a name carrying a space, and sed_inplace read back for its bytes AND its mode. It skips the parity cases OUT LOUD on a bench without readlink -f, because a silent skip is the vacuous pass this whole family was booked for. Fourteen behaviours, wired into shell_dialect_witness.
obs readlink 4 -> 2 with both survivors declared; sed 3 -> 0.
obs The counsel piece writes down the day's sharpest pattern: a meter pointed at a class it was never shaped for reports a fault in the artifact, and the report wears the shape a real one wears. Twice on one day, on two unrelated meters. The danger is that both meters instruct a repair that damages what they measure -- pad the pointer card with prose, strip the explanation out of the self-explaining file -- in the meter's own vocabulary with a number attached.
obs Neither fault was caught by a meter. Both were caught by a reading that could not be true: a C on a page whose four siblings pass, and C-and-B beside register=100, which is impossible for real prose. The practical test is whether the readings describe one artifact.
obs The counsel room was closed 20260821.174047 on Keaton's word, and this piece is written into it on his word of 20260826. Its home under the seated filing test is active-designing, one word away. Named on the piece's own face rather than left for a reader to notice.
obs Writing the adaptation grant into the Dream launcher planted REDS %232's own fault -- a lone apostrophe in "Keaton's word" flips every later character out of the single-quoted prompt, and the printed line died on its next parenthesis. Doubling it repaired the line.
obs The guard written for that fault did not bite, and that is REDS %277. loop_prompt_parse_scan.sh runs tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish by name, one file, typed by hand. Three more printers landed 20260826, one per running star, and none was measured -- so the guard had been blind to three of four from the lap they arrived. Planted the apostrophe deliberately and watched the scan answer zero twice before repairing it.
obs The unmeasured launcher is the one the pier runs unattended overnight, so the first sign would have been a loop printing a syntax error every twenty seconds until a hand looked. Repaired by discovery: the scan now reads every tools/l/launch-*-chapter.rish and prints launcher_read= per tool, 6 runnable lines to 7. The -chapter suffix is load-bearing -- launch-claude.rish and the cursor tools START an agent, so running one in a scan would launch a session rather than measure a string.
loom loop_prompt_parse launchers_before=1 launchers_after=4 runnable_before=6 runnable_after=7
loom shell_portable_control cases=14 parity=6 refusals=3 mode_checks=1
loom dialect readlink_before=4 readlink_after=2 sed_before=3 sed_after=0
